Build **Gantry**, a 3D crane-building puzzle that runs entirely in the browser.

Your project root is `{{workspace}}`. Build the game there.

## Your starting point

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
A TypeScript project is already in place at `{{workspace}}`, and its `README.md`
describes it. Its dependencies are installed, so you can build and test right
away. What is missing is everything under `src/` and everything under `assets/`;
neither directory exists yet. `specs/overview.md` states what you implement and
which files stay as they are.
{{else}}
A TypeScript project is already in place at `{{workspace}}`, and its `README.md`
describes it. Its dependencies are installed, so you can build and test right
away, and `src/main.ts` already stands the engine up over the page's canvas and
runs the game.

What is missing is the game itself, `src/game.ts`, and everything under
